# OneStack mobile — local dev config.
#
# By DEFAULT the app connects to the deployed API on Google Cloud Run (Sydney) — the same backend the
# web app uses. You only need this file to point at a LOCAL API instead. Examples:
#   iOS simulator / web:   http://localhost:3001/api/v1
#   Android emulator:      http://10.0.2.2:3001/api/v1
#   Physical device:       http://<your-machine-LAN-IP>:3001/api/v1
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3001/api/v1
#
# Check-in geolocation: to force/change the location the app sends on check-in (handy for testing on a
# simulator or the web, which have no real GPS), set "latitude,longitude". When set, it overrides real
# GPS. Leave it commented out to use the device's actual location. Example — Melbourne CBD:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_MOCK_LOCATION=-37.8136,144.9631
